; The configuration of the desugar stage.
;
; The stage rewrites a signature into the Eunoia the later stages are written
; over, and almost all of what it does is read off the signature itself. This
; set says the one thing that cannot be: whether a term is the nil of an n-ary
; symbol, where the nil depends on the type of what it terminates.
;
; A symbol declared `:right-assoc-nil` with a *ground* nil needs nothing here
; -- the stage prints the nil and compares -- but one whose nil is of the
; operand's type, as `+` is over the rationals and `bvadd` is over a width,
; needs a predicate, and the stage may not call eo::typeof to write one. So a
; symbol says the predicate under `:is-list-nil` in the set of its own
; semantics, and the programs those compile to are written here rather than
; into the model, which is a later stage than the one that asks.
;
; Compiled by tools/eoc/sem_compile.py, which writes the programs of the
; aggregate below into tools/eoc/out/user_desugar.eo. That file stands where
; the `(include "user_desugar.eo")` of plugins/desugar/eo_desugar.eo names it,
; which is after the signature's own declarations and ahead of the cases that
; call them.

; Whether a term is the nil of an n-ary symbol. Unlike an aggregate of the
; model, the cases of this one are not spliced into one program: the stage
; asks for the predicate of a symbol by name, so each is written out as a
; program of its own, named for the symbol it is of.
(declare-aggregate-method $eo_is_list_nil_)
